[6.775, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.925, "o", "Checked with thomas's own loader, contract, and the canonical Banking77 splits. Verdict: not fit for a fine-tune \u2014 and the main reason isn't the size, it's that this file is your evaluation set.\r\n"]
[7.045, "o", "Two blockers\r\n"]
[7.165, "o", "1. It IS the gonogo canary eval set. The file is an exact prefix (byte-for-byte text+label match) of the canonical pilot: `random.Random(11).sample(test, 250)` with msg-%04d ids, taken from banking77_test.csv. 20/20 rows are eval rows; 0/20 appear in the train set. Fine-tuning on it trains on the thing you score against, so the banked 87.2% [82.5, 90.8] canary number would stop meaning anything. This is contamination, not a small-sample caveat.\r\n"]
[7.285, "o", "2. There's nothing to learn, and the default invocation errors out. 20 rows across 16 labels = 1.25 rows per label (2 labels have 2 rows, 14 have 1). `train_classifier` raises outright: `calib_size=500 must be smaller than the 20 rows given` \u2014 so `modal run -m thomas.encoder_train --data demo-cases.jsonl` fails on shipped defaults before any GPU spend.\r\n"]
[7.405, "o", "What the file does get right\r\n"]
[7.525, "o", "- Shape is contract-valid (\u00a71: `{\"id\"?, \"text\", \"label\"}`): 20 rows parsed, 0 malformed, ids unique and contiguous msg-0000..0019, no empty texts/labels, no exact duplicate texts.\r\n"]
[7.645, "o", "- All 16 labels are real Banking77 categories \u2014 0 unknown against the 77-category universe in the cached CSVs.\r\n"]
[7.765, "o", "- `reverted_card_payment?` (2 rows) is a legitimate Banking77 label, question mark included. Not a typo \u2014 but it's a landmine for any code that strips/sanitizes labels, or that HMACs labels for logging.\r\n"]
[7.885, "o", "- Minor: file is CRLF-terminated (20 CRLF, 0 bare LF). Harmless \u2014 `json.loads` treats the trailing \\r as whitespace.\r\n"]
[8.005, "o", "Also worth stating plainly: at n=20 no paired McNemar can distinguish anything. The smallest detectable one-sided effect is 5.0 points, and only if all 20 cases flip.\r\n"]
[8.125, "o", "If the goal is a real classifier, you already have the material cached locally at ~/git/thomas/examples/data/banking77_train.csv (10,003 rows / 77 labels). `python examples/banking77_encoder.py --dry-run` prints the config and split for free. No Modal call was made here.\r\n"]
[8.245, "o", "If the goal was just \"does this demo file parse as a thomas training input\" \u2014 yes, it parses. It's a valid pilot/demo artifact, just not a training set.\r\n"]
